# =============================================================================
# Trivy scan exceptions — JUSTIFIED, TIME-WINDOWED only.   (policy: Phase 226)
# =============================================================================
#
# HOW THIS WORKS
#   `make scan` passes each finding listed here to Trivy's --ignorefile, so a
#   listed CVE no longer fails the gate UNTIL its `exp:` date, after which Trivy
#   stops ignoring it and the scan fails again — forcing a re-review.
#   Run `make scan-exceptions` to list every entry with days-remaining.
#
# RULES
#   1. NO blanket ignores. One entry per CVE, only when there is genuinely no
#      fix available (anything fixable is patched via apt/apk upgrade instead).
#   2. Every entry MUST have a '#' comment block directly above it (WHY no fix +
#      WHY not exploitable here) and an inline expiry `CVE-XXXX exp:YYYY-MM-DD`.
#   3. Maximum window is 14 days (today + 14d) so exceptions never quietly
#      become permanent.
#
# OPERATOR: ADD / EDIT / DELETE
#   ADD    — append a '#' comment block then `CVE-... exp:<today+14d>`.
#   EDIT   — change the `exp:` date (re-justify in the comment) when extending.
#   DELETE — remove the comment block + CVE line once fixed or resolved.
#   Verify with `make scan-exceptions`. Full guide:
#   docs/runbooks/security_scan_exceptions.md
# =============================================================================


# CVE-2023-24538 / CVE-2023-24540 / CVE-2024-24790 / CVE-2025-68121: Go stdlib CVEs in gosu
# (gosu binary bundled inside redis:7.4.0-alpine, compiled with Go 1.18.2).
# Why no fix: No newer redis:7.4.0-alpine image tag with an updated gosu binary exists.
# Why not exploitable: gosu is a simple setuid+exec wrapper — it does not process HTML
# templates (html/template), parse network addresses (net/netip), nor perform TLS
# session resumption (crypto/tls) in our deployment. The vulnerable code paths in
# Go's statically-linked stdlib are never reached by gosu's runtime.
CVE-2023-24538 exp:2026-07-13
CVE-2023-24540 exp:2026-07-13
CVE-2024-24790 exp:2026-07-13
CVE-2025-68121 exp:2026-07-13

# CVE-2026-31789: OpenSSL heap buffer overflow on 32-bit systems.
# Why no fix: No newer redis:7.4.0-alpine image tag with patched OpenSSL exists.
# Why not exploitable: The vulnerability only affects 32-bit systems. Our deployment
# is on x86_64 (64-bit) hardware. The vulnerable code path is never reachable.
CVE-2026-31789 exp:2026-07-13

# CVE-2026-42504: MIME header DoS in Go stdlib.
# Why no fix: Affects prometheus v3.12.0 and redis_exporter v1.84.0; no newer tags exist that are compiled on Go 1.26.4+.
# Why not exploitable: Neither Prometheus nor redis_exporter parses untrusted MIME headers from external sources in our deployment.
CVE-2026-42504 exp:2026-07-13

# CVE-2026-32280: crypto/tls DoS in Go stdlib.
# Why no fix: Affects node-exporter v1.11.1; no newer release exists.
# Why not exploitable: node-exporter is bound only to loopback (127.0.0.1) and is not exposed to untrusted network traffic.
CVE-2026-32280 exp:2026-07-13

# CVE-2026-45447: Heap Use-After-Free in OpenSSL PKCS7_verify().
# Why no fix: Affects grafana v13.0.2-ubuntu and promtail v3.6.11 (EOL); no newer image tags exist that clear this vulnerability.
# Why not exploitable: PKCS7 verification is not used or triggered in our Grafana/Promtail configuration.
CVE-2026-45447 exp:2026-07-13

