# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964: msgpack out-of-bounds read/crash in test container.
# Why not exploitable: The test container (ja4proxy-test) runs msgpack only for
# JSON serialization of test fixtures; no untrusted msgpack input is processed.
# The test image uses Python 3.14 base; msgpack is pinned transitively via
# dependencies. Fix tracked upstream.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 exp:2026-07-22

# CVE-2026-56123: Heap-based buffer overflow in socat (1.8.0.0–1.8.1.1) in haproxy:2.8.24-alpine.
# Why no fix: haproxy:2.8.24-alpine bundles socat 1.8.1.1-r0; no newer haproxy:2.8.24-alpine
# image tag exists with the patched socat 1.8.1.2-r0. Fix requires upgrading the haproxy
# image tag (tracked separately — upgrade to haproxy:2.8.25-alpine or later).
# Why not exploitable: socat in this image is used only for haproxy admin socket operations
# on a Unix domain socket (/var/run/haproxy.sock). It is not exposed to external network
# input from untrusted clients and is not reachable by the internet-facing attack surface.
CVE-2026-56123 exp:2026-07-11

# CVE-2024-12797: libssl/libcrypto OpenSSL NULL dereference in redis:7.4.0-alpine.
# Why no fix: Fix requires OpenSSL 3.3.3-r0; no newer redis:7.4.0-alpine image tag exists
# with that version of libcrypto3/libssl3.
# Why not exploitable: Redis in our deployment is not configured for client-certificate
# TLS (mTLS), which is the only code path that triggers the NULL dereference in the
# custom certificate-verification callback.
CVE-2024-12797 exp:2026-07-13

# CVE-2022-27664: Go net/http server DoS in gosu binary inside redis:7.4.0-alpine.
# Why no fix: gosu is compiled with Go 1.18.2; no newer redis:7.4.0-alpine image with a
# rebuilt gosu exists. This CVE has been present since 2022 with no upstream fix for the
# bundled binary.
# Why not exploitable: gosu is a one-shot setuid+exec wrapper; it does not run an HTTP
# server, does not listen on any port, and is never called from the network. The vulnerable
# net/http code path is statically linked but completely unreachable at runtime.
CVE-2022-27664 exp:2026-07-13

# CVE-2026-39827: golang.org/x/crypto before 0.52.0 — SSH keep-alive DoS.
# Why no fix: Affects prometheus:v3.12.0, alertmanager:v0.33.0, node-exporter:v1.11.1,
# grafana:13.0.2-ubuntu, loki:3.7.2, and promtail:3.6.11 as a transitive dep compiled
# into each binary. No updated image tags exist for any of these at the required version.
# Why not exploitable: None of these components act as an SSH client or server in our
# deployment. The vulnerable golang.org/x/crypto/ssh code path is statically linked but
# never reachable during normal operation.
CVE-2026-39827 exp:2026-07-13

# CVE-2026-27145: Go stdlib crypto/x509 certificate parsing DoS in grafana:13.0.2-ubuntu.
# Why no fix: Fix requires Go 1.25.11 or 1.26.4; grafana:13.0.2-ubuntu is compiled with
# an older Go version and no newer 13.0.2 image tag exists.
# Why not exploitable: Grafana in our deployment only processes certificates from our own
# PKI (not from untrusted external sources), so maliciously crafted certificates cannot
# reach the vulnerable parsing code.
CVE-2026-27145 exp:2026-07-13

# CVE-2026-39828: golang.org/x/crypto/ssh before 0.52.0 — SSH connection reuse vulnerability.
# Why no fix: Affects prometheus:v3.12.0, alertmanager:v0.33.0, node-exporter:v1.11.1,
# grafana:13.0.2-ubuntu, loki:3.7.2, and promtail:3.6.11 as a transitive dep compiled
# into each binary. No updated image tags that bundle x/crypto ≥ 0.52.0 exist yet.
# Why not exploitable: None of these components act as an SSH client or server in our
# deployment. The vulnerable golang.org/x/crypto/ssh code path is statically linked but
# never reachable during normal operation.
CVE-2026-39828 exp:2026-07-14

# CVE-2026-39829: golang.org/x/crypto/ssh before 0.52.0 — second SSH DoS CVE (sibling of -39828).
# Why no fix: Same affected images as CVE-2026-39828: prometheus:v3.12.0, alertmanager:v0.33.0,
# node-exporter:v1.11.1, grafana:13.0.2-ubuntu, loki:3.7.2, promtail:3.6.11. No updated image
# tags that bundle x/crypto ≥ 0.52.0 exist yet.
# Why not exploitable: None of these components use golang.org/x/crypto/ssh in our deployment.
CVE-2026-39829 exp:2026-07-14

# CVE-2025-15467: OpenSSL libcrypto3 RCE/DoS in redis:7.4.0-alpine (libcrypto3 3.3.2-r0).
# Fix available in 3.3.6-r0 but requires a rebuild of the redis:7.4.0-alpine image by
# the Redis Docker maintainers — no updated tag with the patched Alpine exists yet.
# Why not exploitable: Redis is bound to 127.0.0.1 (loopback only) inside the Docker network
# in our deployment; it is never reachable from external clients. The TLS code path is also
# not enabled in our Redis configuration.
CVE-2025-15467 exp:2026-07-14

# CVE-2022-28131: Go stdlib encoding/xml stack exhaustion in gosu inside redis:7.4.0-alpine.
# Why no fix: gosu is compiled with Go 1.18.2 and bundled in the redis image. No newer
# redis:7.4.0-alpine tag with a rebuilt gosu exists. CVE has been present since 2022.
# Why not exploitable: gosu is a one-shot setuid+exec wrapper that never parses XML; the
# vulnerable encoding/xml code path is statically linked but completely unreachable at runtime.
CVE-2022-28131 exp:2026-07-14

# CVE-2026-39830: golang.org/x/crypto/ssh before 0.52.0 — third SSH DoS CVE (sibling of -39828/-39829).
# Why no fix: Same affected images as -39828/-39829. No updated image tags exist yet.
# Why not exploitable: None of these components use golang.org/x/crypto/ssh in our deployment.
CVE-2026-39830 exp:2026-07-14

# CVE-2025-69421: OpenSSL libcrypto3 PKCS#12 DoS in redis:7.4.0-alpine (libcrypto3 3.3.2-r0).
# Fix in 3.3.6-r0 requires a rebuild of redis:7.4.0-alpine by Docker Redis maintainers.
# Why not exploitable: Redis is loopback-only in our deployment; the PKCS#12 parsing code
# path is never reached by any client-supplied input in our configuration.
CVE-2025-69421 exp:2026-07-14

# CVE-2022-2879: Go stdlib archive/tar memory exhaustion in gosu inside redis:7.4.0-alpine.
# Why no fix: gosu is compiled with Go 1.18.2; no newer redis:7.4.0-alpine tag exists.
# Why not exploitable: gosu never processes tar archives; it is a setuid+exec wrapper only.
CVE-2022-2879 exp:2026-07-14

# CVE-2026-39832: golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/agent before 0.52.0 — fourth in the CVE-2026-3983x batch.
# Affects same images as -39828/-39829/-39830. No updated image tags exist yet.
# Why not exploitable: None of these components use golang.org/x/crypto/ssh in our deployment.
CVE-2026-39832 exp:2026-07-14

# CVE-2026-28387: OpenSSL libcrypto3 arbitrary code execution in redis:7.4.0-alpine (3.3.2-r0).
# Fix in 3.3.7-r0 requires a rebuilt redis:7.4.0-alpine by Docker Redis maintainers.
# Why not exploitable: Redis is loopback-only in our deployment; no untrusted input reaches
# the vulnerable OpenSSL code path.
CVE-2026-28387 exp:2026-07-14

# CVE-2022-2880: Go stdlib net/http/httputil hop-by-hop forwarding in gosu inside redis:7.4.0-alpine.
# Why no fix: gosu is compiled with Go 1.18.2; no newer redis:7.4.0-alpine tag exists.
# Why not exploitable: gosu is a one-shot setuid+exec wrapper that never acts as an HTTP proxy;
# the httputil.ReverseProxy code path is statically linked but never invoked.
CVE-2022-2880 exp:2026-07-14

# ── Redis gosu Go 1.18.2 stdlib CVE batch ───────────────────────────────────
